  "limitations": [
    "The source-to-binary chain is supported by a retained launcher/build log, a clean clone whose 262 recorded inputs independently match the exact git commit, an unchanged retained executable, and matching ELF profile build IDs. This read-only audit did not independently rebuild the executable; go version -m of this test binary does not itself embed the git revision.",
    "The code-input inventory is a declared extension-filtered tracked-file set, not a whole-filesystem or compiler/toolchain/container-image attestation. Selected benchmark workload code and embedded migration SQL are included; cryptographic reproducible-build equivalence is not claimed.",
    "Raw samples independently support sample identities, latencies and arithmetic. PostgreSQL counts and event-gap checks are recorded by the source-bound passing tests; the private schemas and temporary artifact bytes were cleaned up and no full historical database/object dump is retained here.",
    "The three workloads share a development host and PostgreSQL instance with possible concurrent work. Results are finite observations; CPU profiling and GC tracing add overhead, and they are not directly comparable to older GOMAXPROCS32 unprofiled samples.",
    "The scheduler benchmark deliberately stops at claim with 1000 allocations retained until fixture cleanup. Its throughput is not terminal throughput.",
    "Terminal progression is a finite controller invoking real Store/quota/artifact APIs, actual FakeProvider assembly and an in-memory deduplicating executor. It is not application.Driver, native paid-provider, real runner/container, code-repair, crash-recovery or billing-quality evidence. 6000 microUSD and 96000 tokens are synthetic ledger fixtures.",
    "HTTP is 900 reads and 100 admissions through real loopback TCP and nonowner RLS, plus 100 untimed warmup reads. It has no SSE event-size workload and no model/effect execution. It is not k6; quantiles are nearest rank and timing includes client.Do/body drain.",
    "HTTP raw records aggregate pacing and durations but not per-request start times or a separate DB-settings snapshot. Same database environment and matching scheduler/terminal snapshots establish bounded surrounding context; universal stability of all PostgreSQL settings is not proven.",
    "Six raw CPU/heap profiles have independently resolved symbols and the same ELF build ID. Existing heap.top files select alloc_space; this audit additionally selected inuse_space. Profiles include test setup/cleanup and finite GC samples, not a sustained heap-plateau or no-leak proof.",
    "E05/E08/E09 originals retain their historical identity omissions. These new stamped repetitions supplement those workload classes and must not assign their commit, executable hash, processor count, GC settings or latency values to the older runs.",
    "The 85,795,023-byte executable currently remains in the retained /tmp clone, not this versioned result directory; its local availability and digest were independently checked. A future artifact archive should preserve that distinction."
  ],
